Subject: Force OpenTelemetry 1.62.0 for CVE-2026-45292
Description: Force fixed OpenTelemetry artifacts while retaining the version compatible with Quarkus.
Origin: DHI-internal (Nessie CVE remediation)
CVE: CVE-2026-45292
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/projectnessie/nessie 6af26e74f89cf99624328aed2148b1619fa4ce20 servers/quarkus-server/build.gradle.kts
Adaptation: Rebased after the Jackson, Netty, and Reactor force patches in Nessie 0.110.0.
Regenerate: `git apply jackson-core-2.22.3.patch netty-4.2.17.patch reactor-core-3.7.19.patch`, then insert the OpenTelemetry resolution strategy after publishingHelper.
Forwarded: not-needed (DHI Gradle force overlay)
Drop-When: dependency io.opentelemetry:opentelemetry-api >= 1.62.0
Verify: cmd `dhi def build --fast image/nessie/debian-13/0.yaml` expect BUILD SUCCESSFUL; cmd `dhi def sbom image/nessie/debian-13/0.yaml` expect OpenTelemetry 1.62.0 or newer

---
diff --git a/servers/quarkus-server/build.gradle.kts b/servers/quarkus-server/build.gradle.kts
--- a/servers/quarkus-server/build.gradle.kts
+++ b/servers/quarkus-server/build.gradle.kts
@@ -30,6 +30,21 @@
 
 publishingHelper { mavenName = "Nessie - Quarkus Server" }
 
+// CVE-2026-45292 (GHSA-rcgg-9c38-7xpx): unbounded memory allocation in
+// OpenTelemetry W3C baggage propagation, fixed in 1.62.0+. libs.versions.toml
+// declares opentelemetry 1.63.0, but the Quarkus platform BOM can still constrain
+// individual OpenTelemetry jars to an older train. Pin to 1.62.0 (the minimum fixed
+// release): 1.63.0 removes ExporterBuilderUtil.validateEndpoint, which Quarkus 3.37
+// still invokes at startup.
+configurations.configureEach {
+  resolutionStrategy.eachDependency {
+    if (requested.group == "io.opentelemetry" && requested.version?.endsWith("-alpha") != true) {
+      useVersion("1.62.0")
+      because("CVE-2026-45292: force OpenTelemetry 1.62.0 (Quarkus 3.37 compatible, CVE fixed)")
+    }
+  }
+}
+
 // Force reactor-netty to 1.2.18 to resolve CVE-2025-22227 (only fixed in reactor-netty
 // >= 1.2.8). reactor-netty 1.2.x belongs to the Reactor 2024.0 train and requires
 // reactor-core 3.7.x, so reactor-core is pinned to 3.7.19 to keep the train
